{"name":"Let It Rain","hex":"#b6b8bd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"let","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Lesing-Gelimi."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To allow to, not to prevent .","To allow to be or do without interference; to not disturb or meddle with; to leave alone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/let"},{"term":"rain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Condensed water falling from a cloud.","Any matter moving or falling, usually through air, and especially if liquid or otherwise figuratively identifiable with raindrops."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have rain fall from the sky.","To fall as or like rain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Let It Rain (1927 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Let It Rain is a lost 1927 American silent comedy film produced by and starring Douglas MacLean, directed by Edward F. Cline, and featuring Boris Karloff in a minor role as a U.S. mail robber. Paramount Pictures distributed the film. The film is now lost."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/27/Let_It_Rain_FilmPoster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Let_It_Rain_(1927_film)"},{"title":"Let It Rain (2008 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Let It Rain is a 2008 French comedy-drama film directed by Agnès Jaoui from an original screenplay by Jaoui and Jean-Pierre Bacri. It takes its title from the song L'Orage by Georges Brassens, which Jaoui heard on the way to a writing session for the fipm."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cb/Parlez-moi_de_la_pluie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Let_It_Rain_(2008_film)"},{"title":"Let It Rain (Tracy Chapman album)","blocks":[{"text":"Let It Rain is the sixth studio album by American singer-songwriter Tracy Chapman, released on October 15, 2002, by Elektra Records. The album was co-produced by John Parish. It produced two singles: \"You're the One\" and \"Another Sun\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f1/Tracy_Chapman_-_Let_It_Rain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Let_It_Rain_(Tracy_Chapman_album)"},{"title":"Alpha (CL album)","blocks":[{"text":"Alpha is the debut studio album by South Korean rapper and singer CL. It was released on October 20, 2021, through her self-managed label Very Cherry and Sony. Alpha marks CL's first full-length album as a solo artist since her career debut in 2009. The album was preceded by the release of several singles, including \"Spicy\" and \"Lover Like Me\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/15/Alpha_CL_cover.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpha_(CL_album)"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"let":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-let.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-let.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-let.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-let.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-let.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/21/En-us-let.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/21/En-us-let.ogg/En-us-let.ogg.mp3"}],"rain":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/w